\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Credit-assignment rule}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{credit-assignment}

\p{Let #{R} be a rollout record with #{\tau_{\rm stop}} actions, and let #{f} be
its feedback event. A \strong{credit-assignment rule} returns indexed training
targets}

##{\mathsf{Credit}(R,f)=(c_0,\ldots,c_{\tau_{\rm stop}-1}).}

\p{Each #{c_t} is attached to an action or token position declared by the
rule. It may be a return, an advantage estimate, a binary label, or a structured
target. The rule is distinct from the feedback source that supplied #{f}.}
